    {
      "id": "graph-native-membrane-controls-instructions",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Membrane Control Contract Notes",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -220,
        "y": 700
      },
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "right",
          "label": "right",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "bottom",
          "label": "bottom",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        },
        {
          "id": "left",
          "label": "left",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "graph-native-membrane-controls"
        },
        "markdown": "# Membrane control proposal\n\nThe declaration supplies the default membrane behavior. Authored `membrane-control` nodes override it progressively. This is an idea contract, not a claim that the runtime already supports these shapes.\n\n| Controls | Proposed interpretation |\n|---:|---|\n| 0 | Default circle |\n| 1 | Directional stretch / ellipse, if the control carries major-axis semantics |\n| 2 | Axis-defined capsule or two-control procedural shape |\n| 3 | Triangle |\n| 4 | Quadrilateral; square-ish when evenly spaced |\n| N | Polygon, ordered by angle |\n| Advanced | Curved custom membrane using tangents |\n\n## Proposed node fields\n\n`angle` is the radial direction from the owning center. `radius` is a normalized distance, defaulting to 1. `curveBefore?` and `curveAfter?` may later define incoming and outgoing tangents. The owner dimensions and center derive screen coordinates.\n\n`{ \"type\": \"membrane-control\", \"data\": { \"angle\": 45, \"radius\": 1 } }`\n\nFour controls at 45°, 135°, 225°, and 315° can produce a rotated square. Eight evenly spaced controls yield an octagon; changing one radius pulls one corner outward.\n\n## Open design rules\n\nA single control is not a polygon vertex that naturally defines an ellipse. The contract must say whether it denotes a major axis, or require two controls. We also need deterministic ordering, invalid-shape diagnostics, shape-aware clipping, border wrapping, edge attachment, focus behavior, and persistence of dragged controls.\n\nThe value of the model is that membrane geometry becomes inspectable, editable graph structure reusable by users, agents, templates, classes, and later territories."
      },
