      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Declaration Defaults With Progressive Overrides",
        "description": "The declaration defines a default circular membrane. Boundary-control nodes override it progressively: zero controls use the circle; one defines a directional stretch if its semantics are made explicit; two define an axis or capsule; three a triangle; four a quadrilateral; N a polygon. Angle and radius derive normalized radial coordinates; optional before/after tangents enable curves.",
        "differentiator": "The same control primitive supports simple procedural shapes and advanced authored silhouettes without hiding geometry in a renderer blob.",
        "definitionKey": "idea-proposed-approach",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "idea-proposed-approach",
